✗ panic in the container

    warren: a deliberate refusal, raised while composing

  di_test.newPanickingService panicked, in scope "root".
  This is one of two things: a refusal Warren raises on purpose — the
  message above says so when it is — or a bug in the code that panicked.

  READ THE STACK BELOW to see WHICH it is, because this diagnostic
  cannot tell you. The container calls both constructors (at boot, before
  any request) and functions handed to Invoke (which may be a handler,
  mid-request), and it recovers them at the same place. A stack that
  reaches your Handle method is the second kind, and the graph built
  fine — look at the handler, not at your wiring.

